   <row>
    <id><![CDATA[34120]]></id>
    <gid><![CDATA[35476]]></gid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[Your overall preferences]]></group_name>
    <description/>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
    <sid><![CDATA[841423]]></sid>
    <group_order><![CDATA[8]]></group_order>
    <randomization_group/>
    <grelevance><![CDATA[1]]></grelevance>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id><![CDATA[34165]]></id>
    <gid><![CDATA[35509]]></gid>
    <group_name><![CDATA[How Ohbot notices people]]></group_name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p>Before Ohbot says a private reminder out loud, it can check whether someone else is in the room. It could do this in different ways:</p>

<ul>
	<li><b>Microphone only:</b> Ohbot listens for voices.</li>
	<li><b>Camera only:</b> Ohbot turns on the camera on its head and looks around the room.</li>
	<li><b>Microphone first, then camera:</b> Ohbot first listens. Only if it hears no one does it briefly turn on its camera, to make sure that no quiet person (for example someone who is reading) is in the room.</li>
</ul>

<p>In every case, everything is processed on Ohbot; no audio or video recordings are stored. Please rank these ways below.</p>
]]></description>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
    <sid><![CDATA[841423]]></sid>
